  "tradeoffs": [
    "Central utility rooms interrupt the straight courtyard-to-rear-garden sightline. The public rooms connect around them rather than forming the earlier uninterrupted glazed rear band.",
    "The 20 \u00d7 20 ft courtyard is 44% smaller than the former 720 sq ft court. Bedrooms are 18 \u00d7 12.5 ft planning zones; actual side clearances target about 30\u201331 in.",
    "Each ensuite uses a proposed 48 \u00d7 42 in shower and a 24 in wide \u00d7 18 in deep linen cabinet. These dimensional siblings need library publication after layout approval.",
    "Kitchen wing includes an informal four-seat breakfast place; central rear dining remains separate. This gives the kitchen more area than the smaller living room.",
    "Office/guest is L-shaped around the hall bathroom. Its queen bed and work desk are separate; it is not counted as a third dedicated bedroom."
  ],
